From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 22:03:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Build libelf and libdw on Darwin

Mach-O has no alias attribute, so strong_alias gives the definition a
second global name with the assembler's .set directive there. The backends
and libebl use strong_alias or small wrappers instead of spelling the
attribute themselves.

Darwin's C library lacks several GNU extensions. configure now detects
tdestroy, posix_fallocate and program_invocation_short_name:
- eu_tdestroy empties the tree through tdelete when tdestroy is missing.
- elf_update treats posix_fallocate as the space-reservation hint it already
  was, after ftruncate has sized the file.
- getprogname names the program where program_invocation_short_name is
  missing.

gettext is used only when NLS is enabled, and the error fallback carries its
printf format attribute so -Wformat-nonliteral accepts its callers.
